<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela finds condensate oilfield in Maracaibo.</title>
<headline>Venezuela finds condensate oilfield in Maracaibo.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lagoven, a subsidiary of state- owned Petroleos de Venezuela, increased its proven reserves of condensate oil by 13.2 million barrels through the dicovery of a new field in the southern part of Lake Maracaibo, the company said in a press statement.</p>
<p>Initial production from the 5,436 metre exploratory well was 1,270 barrels per day of 45 degree API oil.</p>
<p>In addition to the proven reserves, the find added 9.3 million barrels to probable reserves, Lagoven said.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
